<Project>
  <!--
    go.lib.symbols.targets - Gbtc
    Copyright © 2026 The go2cs Authors. All rights reserved.

    Use of this source code is governed by an MIT-style license
    that can be found in the LICENSE file.

    SYMBOL FILES BESIDE A SINGLE-FILE HOST, ON EVERY PUBLISH.

    The converted runtime reads a frame's file:line from the loose portable PDB of the assembly that holds
    the frame (runtime.Caller, debug.Stack, a panic's traceback), and a single-file publish leaves each
    referenced assembly's .pdb beside the executable. But only the bundler names those files as published
    (its ExcludedFiles), and a publish that finds its bundle up to date skips the bundler, after which the
    SDK's incremental publish clean deletes every one of them as an orphan of the previous publish. Measured
    2026-10-05 on a converted program published twice through its win-x64 profile with nothing changed: 62
    .pdb beside the host after the first publish, 1 after the second (the program's own, which the SDK marks
    ExcludeFromSingleFile itself), and every frame in a dependency then printed with no file:line.

    Marking every published .pdb ExcludeFromSingleFile puts it in the ordinary publish list, the one the
    incremental clean reads, whether or not the bundle runs (measured: 62 kept across two unchanged
    publishes). It changes nothing about what is bundled: a .pdb is never bundled into a single-file host.

    ONE definition, three importers: go.lib.targets (every NuGet consumer of a go.* package), the
    repository's src/Directory.Build.targets (every in-tree project, the -tests hosts included) and the
    Directory.Build.targets that `go2cs -recurse` generates (a module conversion in local-reference mode).
    The guard property keeps a second import inert.

    Inert unless the publish is single-file and not Native AOT. Set GoKeepSymbolsLoose=false to turn it off.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(GoLibSymbolsTargetsImported)' != 'true'">
    <GoLibSymbolsTargetsImported>true</GoLibSymbolsTargetsImported>
    <GoKeepSymbolsLoose Condition="'$(GoKeepSymbolsLoose)' == ''">true</GoKeepSymbolsLoose>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <Target Name="GoKeepSymbolsBesideSingleFileHost"
          AfterTargets="ComputeResolvedFilesToPublishList"
          Condition="'$(GoKeepSymbolsLoose)' == 'true' and '$(PublishSingleFile)' == 'true' and '$(PublishAot)' != 'true'">
    <ItemGroup>
      <ResolvedFileToPublish Update="@(ResolvedFileToPublish)"
                             Condition="'%(ResolvedFileToPublish.Extension)' == '.pdb'"
                             ExcludeFromSingleFile="true" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>
</Project>
